  "subject": "a man who broke the lid of his everyday clay teapot and spends every Sunday at the Fuhe Bridge flea market trying lids from stranger teapots until an old lady sells him one that fits",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien zydeco, Louisiana Creole dancehall style. A piano accordion pumping chords and squeezed riffs; a rubboard frottoir scraping steady sixteenths; electric guitar chicken-picking fills; a bouncing bass; driving backbeat drums. Raw, bright, sweaty live band sound. A raspy male mid-range, cheeky shouting delivery with call-and-response. 124 BPM, D major. Rowdy, stubborn and cheerful. No trap hi-hats, no autotune, no EDM drop, no pop-country gloss, no ballad strings.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n我的茶鈷 用十冬\n蓋仔煞 落塗跤\n碎做三塊 我毋甘\n茶鈷無蓋 茶袂芳\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n拜日透早 我出門\n去福和橋 跳蚤市\n\n[Chorus]\n欠一个蓋仔 欠一个蓋仔\n大的小的 我攏試\n無合 無合 閣再揣\n我毋信 揣無一个\n\n[Verse]\n一攤一攤 我蹲落去\n頭家問我 欲買啥\n我講免啦 借我試\n頭家目睭 共我睨\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n拜日閣來 我閣出門\n茶鈷抱佇 胸坎前\n\n[Chorus]\n欠一个蓋仔 欠一个蓋仔\n圓的扁的 我攏試\n人咧講 這个痟的\n我毋信 揣無一个\n\n[Verse]\n第七拜 一个老阿婆\n伊講少年仔 你過來\n蓋仔崁落 拄拄好\n\n[Bridge]\n伊講五十 我予一百\n我講免找 伊笑一下\n\n[Chorus]\n有一个蓋仔 有一个蓋仔\n茶鈷閣有 伊的帽仔\n透早泡茶 芳甲規厝\n多謝阿婆 拜日閣來\n\n[Outro]\n欠一个蓋仔 這馬無欠矣",
